# Release Process

nft-anndata is a lightweight wrapper around nf-anndata. It is always released **after** a corresponding nf-anndata release. The version numbers should stay in sync.

When the user asks to create a new release, confirm which nf-anndata version this release tracks if not already clear.

## Before releasing — update submodule

Update the nf-anndata submodule pointer to the target release commit (which also pulls in the latest patched jhdf via the nested submodule):

```bash
cd deps/nf-anndata && git fetch origin main && git checkout main && git pull && cd ../..
git add deps/nf-anndata
```

## Files to update

1. **`CHANGELOG.md`** — add a new versioned section referencing the nf-anndata release; leave `## [Unreleased]` empty above it

2. **Run `bump-version.sh`** — handles all other version references in one step:
   ```bash
   ./bump-version.sh <version>
   ```
   This updates `pom.xml`, `src/main/resources/META-INF/nf-test-plugin`, `docs/index.md`, and runs `mvn package`.

## CHANGELOG section format

Since nft-anndata has no independent changes, the entry just references the corresponding nf-anndata release:

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD

- Bump to nf-anndata [X.Y.Z](https://github.com/nictru/nf-anndata/releases/tag/vX.Y.Z)
```
